# Preferences

Add `schemas/` and `prefs.js` only when a task needs a user preference.

- Set `"settings-schema": "org.gnome.shell.extensions.better-gnome-shell"` in `metadata.json`. The schema id is that same string.
- `extension.js` is the only shell code that calls `this.getSettings()`. Pass that `Gio.Settings` object into the features that read it.
- Disconnect settings signals in `disable()` through the feature's `SignalTracker`.

`prefs.js` stays at the extension root because GNOME loads that file by name. It only owns `BetterGnomeShellPreferences`.

Each tab is a named export in its own file under `preferences/`. `generalPage.js` exports `GeneralPage`. Do not define a page class in `prefs.js`. Do not put a second page class in a file that already exports one.

```javascript
export default class BetterGnomeShellPreferences extends ExtensionPreferences {
    fillPreferencesWindow(window) {
        const settings = this.getSettings();

        window.add(new GeneralPage());
        window.add(new PanelPage(settings));
        window.add(new DockPage(settings));
    }
}
```

A new tab is a new file. `prefs.js` imports that class and adds it to the window.

A subpage follows the same rule: its own file under `preferences/`, imported and added by the parent page. A subpage does not import a sibling page. When two pages need the same helper, move that helper to its own file under `preferences/`.
